WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.340
Once source material is gathered, AI can help extract and normalize security-relevant facts.

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:20.280
Candidate items include assets, services, endpoints, data stores, identities, protocols, queues, integrations, external dependencies, owners, and environments.

3
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:27.020
The model can turn narrative notes into structured tables and can highlight fields that appear to be missing or inconsistent.

4
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.980
Normalization is a practical challenge.

5
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:37.720
One source may call a component payment-api, another may call it Payments Service, and a diagram may label it Checkout Backend.

6
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.340
AI can help group likely matches, but reviewers should confirm whether names refer to the same component.

7
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.720
Deduplication is useful only when it is evidence-backed.

8
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.020
Merging unrelated items can hide important risk.

9
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.100
Structured outputs should preserve provenance.

10
00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:03.680
A component table is much more trustworthy when each row can point back to a README, diagram, manifest, inventory export, ticket, or owner confirmation.

11
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:12.660
Provenance lets reviewers verify statements, resolve disagreement, and update the record later when source material changes.

12
00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.220
AI is also useful for asking clarifying questions.

13
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.480
If an API appears in one file but not in the architecture diagram, the model can flag the mismatch.

14
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.380
If a storage bucket exists without an owner, the model can create an open item.

15
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:36.200
If a trust boundary is implied but not documented, the model can ask what identity, network, or data control separates the contexts.

16
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:43.840
The rule is simple: AI may organize, summarize, and suggest, but it should not silently invent.

17
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.460
Missing facts should become visible uncertainty.

18
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:53.880
That habit makes the documentation more useful because it shows both what the team knows and what still needs validation.
